  "id": "55eb63c2-d1a1-4c54-9489-4762f96c2c6d",
  "title": "T2T-VICL: Cross-Task Visual In-Context Learning via Implicit Text-Driven VLMs",
  "summary": "T2T-VICL bridges the gap between visual tasks by using implicit text-driven prompts to align VLMs with diverse cross-task relations, offering a lightweight solution for improving task-aware alignment across mismatched examples.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "T2T-VICL uses a collaborative prompt-transfer framework to convert mismatched visual demonstrations into implicit text guidance.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "It constructs a dataset of implicit cross-task relations from structured descriptions of visual changes and task differences.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Experiments show that T2T-VICL improves task-aware alignment and image fidelity compared to fixed prompting and other methods.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
